#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:1
msgid "Native Instruments Traktor Kontrol S4 MK3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:3
msgid ""
"The Kontrol S4 MK3 is a 4 deck all-in-one controller with a sturdy build "
"quality and integrated sound card. Compared to the MK2 and MK1, it also have"
" motorised shiny aluminum jogwheels, screens and a set of pads which can be "
"use for various features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:7
msgid ""
"The S4 MK3 uses the standard {term}`HID` protocol for the Buttons, Knobs, "
"Faders and LEDs, and extends it for the motorized Jog-Wheels. The screens "
"use a USB Bulk transfer. Mixxx doesn't support rendering content for "
"external screens yet. The easiest way to tell the MK3 apart from the other "
"MK1 and 2 are these screens, displace between the \"Move\" and \"Loop\" "
"encoder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:11
msgid ""
"Unlike its predecessor, the Kontrol S4 Mk3 cannot run from {term}`USB` power"
" and the separate power supply must be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:13
msgid ""
"[Manufacturer’s product page](https://www.native-"
"instruments.com/en/products/traktor/dj-controllers/traktor-kontrol-s4/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:18
msgid "Added beatjump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:21
msgid "Added stems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:24
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:26
msgid ""
"The Kontrol S4 MK3 is a USB class compliant audio and {term}`HID`, so it is "
"compatible with Mixxx without any proprietary drivers on GNU/Linux, MacOS "
"and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:28
msgid ""
"With the S4 plugged in, a HID device is listed as an available controller in"
" Mixxx’s Preferences. The controller uses HID for each components on the "
"device, except the screens, so the mapping can only be loaded when you "
"select the HID device on the left side of Mixxx’s Preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:31
msgid "Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:33
msgid "Setup audio output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:35
msgid "Using the S4 mixer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:37
msgid ""
"In order to use the audio output of the controller, select the device "
"{guilabel}`Traktor Kontrol S4 MK3`. {guilabel}`Channels 1 - 2` should be set"
" as {guilabel}`Main` and {guilabel}`Channels 3 - 4` should be set as "
"{guilabel}`Headphones`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:39
msgid "Using the software mixer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:41
msgid ""
"If you don't want to use certain outputs of the device, you can enable the "
"mapping of the mixer knob to the Mixxx internal mixer. Head over to the "
"{ref}`settings` to enable these optional mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:44
msgid ""
"The mixer knobs are physically linked to the S4 embedded mixer. This means "
"that there is no way to prevent these buttons to adjust gains of the output,"
" and will lead to unexpected volume mixing if the Mixxx mixer is used while "
"also using S4 outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:48
msgid "Known bugs and limitation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:50
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:52
msgid ""
"During the development phase, it appears that using other Sound API than "
"_ALSA_ would lead the Master VU meter not to work. Furthermore, audio output"
" power would be half as loud as it should be, which can be a problem if you "
"are also using other software, since you audio setting will suddenly become "
"twice as loud. It remains unclear whether or not this was a common issue or "
"if this was specific to the used setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:56
msgid "Screens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:58
msgid ""
"Currently, Mixxx doesn't support controller screen rendering. However, "
"because the screens are technically a different device, it is safe to "
"interact with them outside of Mixxx while the device is being used by Mixxx."
" This can be particularly handy if you want to display some images or text, "
"or even dynamic information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:63
msgid "Motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:65
msgid ""
"Haptic feedback (know as Haptic Drive (TM)) are partially implemented. "
"Supported features include jogwheel tensions and turntable mode but these "
"features remains in beta and may sometime have unexpected behaviours. Since "
"there is no guarantee on the long term effect to the controller of how Mixxx"
" implements these features, they are disabled by default. You can enable "
"them by setting _UseMotors_ to `true` in {ref}`settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:70
msgid "Mapping Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:74
msgid "Jogwheel modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:76
msgid ""
"Jogwheel can be used to control various things, depending of the mode they "
"are in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:78
msgid ""
"**Vinyl mode** (*default*): The jogwheel platter can be used for scratch. "
"The jogwheel crown can be used to jog up or down the playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:79
msgid ""
"**Jog mode**: The wheel platter and crown can be used to jog up or down the "
"playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:80
msgid ""
"**Turntable mode**: The wheel behaves as a 33.3 RPM turntable. If the "
"platter or crown are slowed down or speeded up, then it will scratch down or"
" up the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:83
msgid ""
"Because this mode relies on Mixxx's scratch mode, if the track has been "
"pitched up, the keylock will be ignored!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:87
msgid ""
"This mode is only available if the motor features are enabled. See "
"{ref}`use-motors` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:90
msgid ""
"**Loop in**: The wheel behaves similarly to CDJ. If the platter or crown are"
" turned, it will move back or forth the start of the loop. Additionally, if "
"the loop encoder is used, it will move the all loop back or forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.md:91
msgid ""
"**Loop out**: Like for the **loop in** mode, but with the exit position of "
"the loop. If the platter or crown are turned, it will move back or forth the"
" end of the loop. Additionally, if the loop encoder is used in the same way "
"than **Loop in** mode."
msgstr ""

